  "spans": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "LESSON PURPOSE\n",
      "size": 22,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Goal: apply “Essential Rust crates: what they do and who maintains them” to a real program or device. The key principle is: Serde's derive serializes the fields; ",
      "size": 17,
      "color": "#212121"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "serde_json",
      "size": 17,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " produces JSON and must be added to Cargo. In a project, follow this guidance: For the Serde example, run ",
      "size": 17,
      "color": "#212121"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "cargo add serde --features derive",
      "size": 17,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " and ",
      "size": 17,
      "color": "#212121"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "cargo add serde_json",
      "size": 17,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "; read the crate docs and keep secrets out of source code.\n\n",
      "size": 17,
      "color": "#212121"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "QUESTION: What will this example do? Predict the result first.\n",
      "size": 16,
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "EXAMPLE CODE\n",
      "size": 20,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "diagram",
      "id": "rust_serde_flow",
      "caption": "Essential Rust crates: what they do and who maintains them"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "rust",
      "code": "use serde::Serialize;\n#[derive(Serialize)]\nstruct Reading { name: String, score: u8 }\nfn main() -> Result<(), serde_json::Error> {\n    let reading = Reading { name: \"Ada\".into(), score: 10 };\n    println!(\"{}\", serde_json::to_string(&reading)?);\n    Ok(())\n}",
      "showCopyButton": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "EXPECTED RESULT\n",
      "size": 20,
      "color": "#2E7D32",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Serde serializes the value as ",
      "size": 16,
      "color": "#2E7D32"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "{\"name\":\"Ada\",\"score\":10}",
      "size": 16,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": ".\n\n",
      "size": 16,
      "color": "#2E7D32"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "CORE EXPLANATION\n",
      "size": 20,
      "color": "#6A1B9A",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "A Rust crate provides reusable code; add it to ",
      "size": 17
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Cargo.toml",
      "size": 17,
      "bold": true,
      "color": "#1565C0"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": ", then import it with ",
      "size": 17
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "use",
      "size": 17,
      "bold": true,
      "color": "#1565C0"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": ". ",
      "size": 17
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "serde",
      "size": 17,
      "bold": true,
      "color": "#1565C0"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " reads and writes formats such as JSON; it was created by David Tolnay and is maintained with open-source contributors. ",
      "size": 17
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "tokio",
      "size": 17,
      "bold": true,
      "color": "#1565C0"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " is a runtime for asynchronous servers and network work; Carl Lerche started the project, which is maintained by its community. ",
      "size": 17
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "clap",
      "size": 17,
      "bold": true,
      "color": "#1565C0"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " parses command-line options, ",
      "size": 17
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "reqwest",
      "size": 17,
      "bold": true,
      "color": "#1565C0"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " sends HTTP requests, and ",
      "size": 17
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "embedded-hal",
      "size": 17,
      "bold": true,
      "color": "#1565C0"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " defines shared interfaces for microcontroller drivers. The standard library ships with Rust; these crates are separate dependencies. Check versions, licenses, compatibility, and security updates.\n\nExample Cargo.toml dependencies: ",
      "size": 17
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "tokio = { version = \"1\", features = [\"macros\", \"rt-multi-thread\", \"time\"] }",
      "size": 17,
      "bold": true,
      "color": "#1565C0"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": ", ",
      "size": 17
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "serde = { version = \"1\", features = [\"derive\"] }",
      "size": 17,
      "bold": true,
      "color": "#1565C0"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": ", ",
      "size": 17
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "serde_json = \"1\"",
      "size": 17,
      "bold": true,
      "color": "#1565C0"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": ", ",
      "size": 17
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "anyhow = \"1\"",
      "size": 17,
      "bold": true,
      "color": "#1565C0"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": ", ",
      "size": 17
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "thiserror = \"2\"",
      "size": 17,
      "bold": true,
      "color": "#1565C0"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": ", and ",
      "size": 17
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "embedded-hal = \"1\"",
      "size": 17,
      "bold": true,
      "color": "#1565C0"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": ". Tokio supplies an async runtime and timers; Serde provides format-independent serialization; ",
      "size": 17
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "anyhow",
      "size": 17,
      "bold": true,
      "color": "#1565C0"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " adds application-level error context; ",
      "size": 17
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "thiserror",
      "size": 17,
      "bold": true,
      "color": "#1565C0"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " helps define typed library errors; and ",
      "size": 17
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "embedded-hal",
      "size": 17,
      "bold": true,
      "color": "#1565C0"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " defines portable driver traits over a board-specific HAL. These projects are maintained by the Tokio team, Serde community, and Rust Embedded Working Group. ",
      "size": 17
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "embedded-hal",
      "size": 17,
      "bold": true,
      "color": "#1565C0"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " alone does not control physical GPIO; a chip/board HAL implements the traits.\n\n",
      "size": 17
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "IMPORTANT LINE BREAKDOWN\n",
      "size": 20,
      "color": "#6A1B9A",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Key line: ",
      "size": 16
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "let reading = Reading { name: \"Ada\".into(), score: 10 };",
      "size": 16,
      "bold": true,
      "color": "#1565C0"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "\nWhat it does: Serde's derive serializes the fields; ",
      "size": 16
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "serde_json",
      "size": 16,
      "bold": true,
      "color": "#1565C0"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " produces JSON and must be added to Cargo.\nWhy it is used: For the Serde example, run ",
      "size": 16
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "cargo add serde --features derive",
      "size": 16,
      "bold": true,
      "color": "#1565C0"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " and ",
      "size": 16
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "cargo add serde_json",
      "size": 16,
      "bold": true,
      "color": "#1565C0"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "; read the crate docs and keep secrets out of source code.\nIf omitted or changed: Library choice depends on the target: ",
      "size": 16
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "embedded-hal",
      "size": 16,
      "bold": true,
      "color": "#1565C0"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " serves microcontroller drivers, while Tokio targets general asynchronous I/O.\n\n",
      "size": 16
    },
    {
      "type": "detail",
      "title": "Common mistake",
      "text": "Crate APIs and feature flags can change; commit Cargo.lock for applications and test examples with your toolchain."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "REMEMBER\n",
      "size": 19,
      "color": "#00897B",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Serde's derive serializes the fields; ",
